WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:05.410
Speaker 1: Yesterday, there was some very
interesting hearings in Washington, D.C.,

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:08.809
sort of primarily about the Janet what happened
on January 6th.

00:00:08.809 --> 00:00:12.440
And a little bit later, we're going to get
to the comments from Donald Trump's former

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:19.659
acting secretary of defense about when Donald
Trump finally did say, OK, let's bring in

00:00:19.659 --> 00:00:23.269
the National Guard to clean up what's going
on on January 6th.

00:00:23.269 --> 00:00:24.729
We'll get to that later.

00:00:24.729 --> 00:00:28.259
But one of the really interesting I don't
know if we would call it a side story.

00:00:28.259 --> 00:00:33.130
It's really kind of a main story that came
out yesterday during the testimony is that

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:38.940
the Biden administration's top law enforcement
officials, including Merrick Garland, the

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:45.260
attorney general, including Homeland Security
Secretary Mayorkas and a number of others,

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:54.530
they said in no uncertain terms that white
supremacists are the greatest domestic terrorist

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.510
threat within the United States.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:01:01.379
Now, if you've been watching my show for a
while or if you're familiar with the data

00:01:01.379 --> 00:01:05.070
on domestic terrorism, this would not be a
surprise to you.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:12.979
The story that the right has been telling
for a very long time is that American Muslims

00:01:12.979 --> 00:01:18.979
or immigrants from Muslim countries, even
left wing ecoterrorists in some versions of

00:01:18.979 --> 00:01:22.450
the story, are really the great domestic threat.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:27.560
But when you look at the data and you look
at domestic extremism incidents, you very

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:34.399
quickly understand that the biggest threat
in the United States indeed, is white supremacists,

00:01:34.399 --> 00:01:39.450
which sometimes overlap with these sort of
patriot and sovereign citizen antigovernment

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.229
type movements.

00:01:41.229 --> 00:01:43.500
That's really where the bulk of the threat
comes from.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:48.979
And Merrick Garland said yesterday to lawmakers,
quote, Domestic violent extremists pose an

00:01:48.979 --> 00:01:51.610
elevated threat in twenty twenty one and in.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:59.289
The FBI's view, the top domestic violent extremist
threat we face comes from racially or ethnically

00:01:59.289 --> 00:02:06.429
motivated violent extremists, specifically
those who advocate for the superiority of

00:02:06.429 --> 00:02:08.350
the white race.

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:15.720
Now, what you are also starting to see is
that Republicans are having to find a new

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:18.590
way to even talk about this.

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:25.500
And Senator Richard Shelby, for example, instead
of focusing on the level of threat, is trying

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.920
to make the administration seemed biased in
its priorities.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:35.110
And when it was Richard Shelby's turn to talk
to Merrick Garland, he asked, are you investigating,

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:42.190
for example, the protests in Portland, Oregon,
with the same vigor that you're investigating

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:44.220
what happened on January 6th?

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:50.090
The implication and wrapped up in that is
the implication and the assumption that the

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:56.590
Portland protests were left wing violence,
whereas I guess he sort of may be conceding

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:59.870
that the January 6th riots were right wing
violence.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:04.900
And Merrick Garland responded very well and
said, quote, We don't care what the ideology

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:05.900
is.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:07.970
Violations of law are pursued and are prosecuted.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:11.261
I think it's fair to say that in my career
as a judge and in law enforcement, I have

00:03:11.261 --> 00:03:16.400
not seen a more dangerous threat to democracy
than the invasion of the Capitol.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.920
That doesn't mean we don't focus on other
threats as well.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:24.230
And so we we are starting to see this kind
of shift among the right, where it's becoming

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:30.300
essentially undeniable that the bulk of the
incidents are these right wing patriot, sovereign

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:37.040
citizen, anti-government and certainly white
supremacist, racially, ethnically, religiously

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.950
motivated events.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:42.140
But what Republicans are now kind of going
back to and it's good that they're having

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:45.350
to change what they're saying, even though
it's still bogus, is OK.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:48.640
Well, maybe these are the numbers, but what
about the attention that's being paid?

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:52.430
There are political decisions that are being
made about who to investigate, who to charge,

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:53.430
et cetera.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:56.070
And that should be and that should be looked
into.

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:58.370
But it's sort of like a welcome to our world
moment.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:02.170
This is what many of us have been saying about
the judicial justice system for a very, very

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:03.230
long time.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:11.820
When you look at who actually does drugs,
has drugs, deals, drugs versus who is prosecuted,

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:15.730
who is policed, what are the sentences that
are given out?

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:19.400
We've been pointing out that there's a lack
of equity there for a very long time along

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:23.920
racial lines for sure, among class lines as
well as we've discussed.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:31.150
So now unable to continue denying the empirical
reality of where the greatest number of threats

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:35.740
come from, they are pushed back to having
to make an argument the left has been making

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:38.440
about the justice system for a very long time.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:42.419
I don't know where this will go, but yesterday's
hearings were very interesting because they

00:04:42.419 --> 00:04:46.460
touched on a lot of these different tangential
topics.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:53.370
They're big topics, but tangential to the
to the day of January 6th, including investigative

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:57.969
priorities for federal law enforcement, including
what the biggest threats are.

00:04:57.969 --> 00:05:02.569
And a little bit later in the show, we will
get to some of the testimony about the nitty

00:05:02.569 --> 00:05:05.749
gritty of what happened on January 6th.

